# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/
# Per-run state written by tools/doc_freshness_cron.sh: the commit it last
# checked. Tracking it would dirty the tree every night and conflict on every
# merge. An agent worktree committed it once; that is what this prevents.
.beads/.doc-freshness-last

# Alternative backends and diagnostic builds of the game binary. Anchored with a
# leading slash so it matches only the repository root: unanchored, a gitignore
# pattern matches at every level, and this one silently swallowed
# docs/media/incursion-macos.png.
/incursion-*

# ...but NOT the shipped readme. Git matches this pattern case-insensitively on a
# case-insensitive filesystem, so /incursion-* swallowed Incursion-macOS.txt --
# which tools/package_macos_app.sh copies into the bundle and tools/check_app.sh
# requires, so a fresh clone would have failed to build a release. Second time
# this pattern has eaten a real file; the first was docs/media/incursion-macos.png.
!/Incursion-macOS.txt

# Release artifacts, produced by tools/package_macos.sh.
dist/

# Credentials. None of these has ever been committed; these lines exist so a
# stray copy cannot be. The real notarisation credential lives at
# ~/.config/incursion/notary.env, outside this tree, written mode 600 by
# tools/setup_notary.sh.
*.p12
*.pem
*.cer
*.pfx
*.mobileprovision
*.env
notary.env
.netrc
id_rsa
id_ed25519

# Agent worktrees. `git worktree add` puts a real checkout here, so without this
# line `git status` in the main tree offers to commit a second copy of the whole
# repository. The worktrees themselves are disposable; their branches carry the
# work.
.claude/worktrees/

# One-off overnight run reports and their working papers. Both were tracked once
# and should not have been: MORNING-REPORT.md is a dated report of a single
# 2026-08-20 job, nothing in the tree references it, and once tracked it acquired
# a citation header that enlisted it in a checker that must stay green forever.
# docdelta/ is that job's scratch output; its findings live in beads and its
# dependency lists were merged into docs/doc-deps.tsv, which IS tracked.
MORNING-REPORT.md
docdelta/
